Gaming Leaderboard Management System
 Introduction
 The Gaming Leaderboard Management System is a database-powered application 
that keeps track of player performance across different competitions. In the world 
of competitive gaming, having accurate records of players and their scores is 
crucial for fair rankings and transparent results. Relying on manual tracking often 
leads to mistakes and becomes inefficient, especially when managing multiple 
players and tournaments at once.
 To solve this, the project applies Database Management System (DBMS) concepts 
to build a structured and dependable platform. It stores player details, competition 
data, and scores in a relational database, ensuring both accuracy and easy access. 
On top of that, a user-friendly web interfacedeveloped with PHP, HTML, and 
CSSlets users view leaderboards in real time. Players are ranked automatically 
based on their scores, making the system both efficient and reliable.
 Project  overview
 Description of the Gaming Leaderboard Management System
 The Gaming Leaderboard Management System is a web-based application that 
combines a relational database with a simple, user-friendly interface to manage and 
display player rankings in gaming competitions. It was developed as a practical 
example of how DBMS concepts can address real-world challenges in competitive 
environments where accurate score tracking and fair rankings are essential.
 At its core, the system uses a MySQL database designed with a normalized schema 
to reduce redundancy and maintain consistency. The database is built around three 
main entitiesPlayers, Competitions, and Scoreswith relationships that allow 
data to be stored and retrieved efficiently. Since players can join multiple 
competitions, their performance records in the Scores table serve as the foundation 
for calculating leaderboards.
On the frontend, HTML and CSS handle structure and design, while PHP manages 
the backend logic, connecting to the database and dynamically fetching 
leaderboard data.
 Explanation of the Role of the Database in Supporting the Management 
System:
 The database is the backbone of the Gaming Leaderboard System, ensuring accurate 
and efficient management of data. Its role can be summarized in three main points:
 1. Data Storage & Integrity – Stores players, competitions, and scores in a 
structured way, maintaining consistency with primary and foreign keys.
 2. Dynamic Leaderboard Generation – Uses SQL queries to rank players 
automatically, with updates reflected instantly on the leaderboard.
 3. Scalability & Flexibility – The schema can be easily extended to support more 
players, competitions, and future features like authentication or statistics.
 Requirements Analysis
 The Requirements Analysis identifies the key functionalities and system needs for 
the Gaming Leaderboard Management System. It ensures that both the database 
