 Normalization Process and Resulting Schema Design
 The database design follows the normalization process to remove redundancy and 
ensure data integrity:
  First Normal Form (1NF)
 Ensures that all attributes contain atomic (indivisible) values.
 Example: Player entity has single-valued attributes like Player_Name, Email, etc.
  Second Normal Form (2NF)
 Ensures no partial dependency on composite keys.
 Since Player_ID and Competition_ID are stored separately in Score, there are no 
partial dependencies.
  Third Normal Form (3NF)
 Ensures no transitive dependency between non-key attributes.
 Example: In Score, Score_Value determines Rank, but since ranking is 
dynamically generated, it is acceptable and does not create redundancy.
