 Sample Queries
 Query 1: Display Matches for a Specific Player
 SELECT P.Name, SUM(S.Points) AS TotalScore
 FROM Score S
 JOIN Player P ON S.PlayerID = P.PlayerID
 GROUP BY P.PlayerID
 ORDER BY TotalScore DESC
 LIMIT 5;
Query 2: Top 3 players overall
 SELECT 
 p.username AS Player, 
 SUM(m.score) AS TotalScore
 FROM matches m
 JOIN players p ON m.player_id = p.id
 GROUP BY p.id
 ORDER BY TotalScore DESC
 Limitations and Future Works
 Limitations
 ➢ Scalability Issues
 The current system may not efficiently handle very large numbers of players or 
competitions if the database size grows significantly. Query performance might 
degrade without proper indexing or optimization.
 ➢ Real-Time Updates
 The leaderboard may not always reflect real-time updates if data refresh is delayed 
or if heavy traffic occurs during peak gaming sessions.
 ➢ Security Concerns
 Basic authentication and data validation are implemented, but advanced security 
measures such as encryption, intrusion detection, or protection against SQL injection 
may not be fully developed.Also passwords are weak for experimental purpose.
 ➢ Limited Analytics
The system primarily focuses on storing and displaying scores. It does not yet 
provide in-depth analytics, such as player performance trends, win/loss ratios, or 
predictive insights.
 ➢ Device and Platform Dependency
 The current design may be optimized for web-based access only. Mobile and cross
platform support may be limited or absent.
 ➢ Customization Restrictions
 Game developers or administrators may have limited ability to customize ranking 
criteria, scoring rules, or leaderboard visualization.
 Future Work:
 1. Database Optimization and Scalability
 Implement advanced indexing, caching strategies, and distributed database 
solutions to handle larger player bases and ensure faster queries.
 2. Real-Time Leaderboard
 Introduce WebSocket or streaming-based updates so that players can view live 
score changes without refreshing the page.
 3. Enhanced Security Features
 Add role-based access control (RBAC), encrypted data storage, and two-factor 
authentication to ensure system security.
 4. Advanced Analytics and Insights
 Integrate data visualization tools and AI-based analysis to provide deeper 
insights into player performance and competition dynamics.
 5. Mobile and Cross-Platform Support
 Develop mobile-friendly interfaces and APIs that allow integration with mobile 
apps, consoles, or third-party gaming platforms.
6. Gamification Features
 Add badges, achievements, seasonal rankings, and reward systems to increase 
player engagement and competitiveness.
 7. Integration with External System
 Provide APIs for integrating with external games, payment systems, or cloud 
services for broader usability.
 Conclusion
 The Gaming Leaderboard System demonstrates how Database Management 
System (DBMS) principles can be applied to create a functional and interactive 
platform for managing players, competitions, and scores. Built with MySQL as the 
backend and PHP, HTML, and CSS for the frontend, the system supports real-time 
data handling and dynamic updates, such as recording scores and generating live 
leaderboards.
 Key Achievements
 • Secure login system for both players and administrators.
 • Efficient data storage and retrieval through relational tables (Players, 
Competitions, and Scores).
 • Instant leaderboard updates, reflecting score changes as soon as they are 
entered by admins.
 • User-friendly interface with a clean, visually appealing design for easy 
navigation across competitions, matches, and player stats.
 Overall, the project highlights the role of data integrity, dynamic web design, and 
user interactivity in building reliable database-driven applications. Looking ahead, 
it can be enhanced with features such as competition-specific leaderboards, 
detailed player profiles, and analytics, making it a scalable solution for modern 
gaming communities.
